    <h1>Privacy Policy for AlphaSteps</h1>
    <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> 20 April 2026</p>

    <p>AlphaSteps ("we", "our", or "us") respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect your information when you use our mobile application.</p>

    <hr>

    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

    <h3>a) User Information</h3>
    <p>- Username or nickname (if entered by the user)</p>

    <h3>b) Usage Data</h3>
    <p>- Game progress (scores, answers, leaderboard position)<br>
       - Interaction with app features</p>

    <h3>c) Device Information</h3>
    <p>- Device type<br>
       - Operating system<br>
       - App version</p>

    <hr>

    <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
    <p>
        - Provide and improve app functionality<br>
        - Display leaderboard rankings<br>
        - Enhance user experience<br>
        - Fix bugs and improve performance
    </p>

    <hr>

    <h2>3. Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>Our app uses third-party services such as Firebase (Google) for authentication and database.</p>

    <p>Learn more:<br>
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank">
        https://policies.google.com/privacy
    </a></p>

    <hr>

    <h2>4. Data Security</h2>
    <p>
        - Data is transmitted securely (encrypted in transit)<br>
        - Access to data is limited and controlled
    </p>

    <hr>

    <h2>5. Data Sharing</h2>
    <p>We do NOT sell or rent user data. Data is only used to operate the app.</p>

    <hr>

    <h2>6. Children’s Privacy</h2>
    <p>AlphaSteps is designed for general audiences, including students. We do not knowingly collect personal data without safeguards.</p>

    <hr>

